  "goodToKnow": "Die Eingeweide are entrails or intestines, mostly of animals and in anatomy; it's plural in normal use. Figuratively, they're the inner workings of a machine or building. Edible organs are Innereien (offal). The intestine itself is der Darm. Mir drehen sich die Eingeweide um means something makes me feel sick, physically or morally."
